    {
      "reason": "The deployed route returns HTTP 200 text/csv. history_csv.py:99–122 emits the fixed header, CRLF, exact UTF-8 bytes with no BOM, literal quoted account IDs, decimal integer fields and relative direction. The HTTP contract probe verified incoming and outgoing row values, non-ASCII and quoted identifiers, large integer amount, header-only empty history, and the exact account-not-found JSON 404. history_csv.py:53–92 retains the original fractional digits while normalizing the whole time to UTC, including timestamps with a short year. Independent filtered and unfiltered HTTP probes reproduced the stored .654321Z value exactly. The supplemental dot-fraction check also preserved .654321987Z.",
      "requirement": "REQ-CSV-01",
      "verdict": "pass"
    },
    {
      "reason": "repository.py:86–94 selects related rows using one OR predicate and orders by SQLite integer ID, which emitted both roles and excluded unrelated transfers in the independent replay. history_csv.py:95–110 selects direction relative to the account, uses source precedence for a self-transfer, and applies both date bounds independently and inclusively after UTC normalization. The public probes confirmed day boundaries with fractional seconds, the extreme years including a legacy short-year row, combining filters, and the standard JSON 422 errors for invalid or reversed ranges. The pre/post SQLite dumps matched and service.py:49–53 uses a read session with account lookup and SELECT only.",
      "requirement": "REQ-CSV-02",
      "verdict": "pass"
    }
